ers split between Tossup and a narrow Democratic lean, a small Acton edge with substantial uncertainty is the best read.", "watch": "Ramaswamy's heavy spending advantage and any late consolidation of Republican-leaning voters could erase Acton's narrow polling lead before Election Day.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike DeWine (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Ohio's open governor's race pairs Democrat Amy Acton against Republican Vivek Ramaswamy after two terms of Mike DeWine, who is term-limited. Polling through early October consistently shows Acton slightly ahead: high-quality surveys from NYT/Siena, Marist, and Suffolk give her leads of four to nine points, while a Republican-sponsored poll found a one-point Ramaswamy edge. Averaged together, recent polls put Acton up roughly four points.\n\nThe race remains genuinely competitive. Ohio leans Republican by about five points, Ramaswamy has raised far more money, and most expert raters call the contest a tossup, though prediction markets give Acton about a two-in-three chance. Ramaswamy's advertising edge and any late movement among Republican-leaning voters are the main paths to a closer finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.545, "margin": 0.49}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5929, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5919, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6166, "margin": 1.3}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5684, "margin": 1.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.592, "margin": 1.4}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6233, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.662, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6672, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6954, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6965, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7208, "margin": 2.7}]}